 ${python3:Depends},
 openssh-sftp-server,
 python3-yaml,
 sudo,
Description: privileged mutations of a Frikanalen media archive
 The ingest engine writes into the media archive over SSH. Rather than giving
 the account it logs in as write access to the archive, this package installs
 the three mutations it actually performs -- publish a file, trash a directory,
 or delete one explicitly allowed regenerable variant -- as commands that run
 as the account owning the archive, reached through a single sudoers rule.
 .
 Two more ship as operator tools with their own entry points, deliberately
 outside what that rule grants: fk-archive-purge-trash, which is the only thing
 here that may destroy material which cannot be rebuilt from the original, and
 fk-archive-migrate-broadcast, a one-shot migration of a video's source out of
 the directory the previous system kept it in.
 .
 Every command validates the paths it is given against the archive's namespace,
 traverses it without following symbolic links, and refuses to overwrite
 anything. General removal is a rename into .trash/; permanent variant deletion
 is restricted by an allowlist.
